From bd164c1d96132a70e0e750b2178d7362dfe01663 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:28:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 077/120] fix(crypto): encrypted GUI backups use the keyed
 digest; Service Mode reads get the key (issue #13)

Encrypted directory backups made by the GUI and the service could not be
read back, neither by Nimbus nor by proxmox-backup-client.

Wrong chunk digest: ChunkState (gui/backup_inline.go) hashed every chunk
with a bare sha256, ignoring the key. The chunks were encrypted but
indexed under sha256(plaintext) instead of sha256(plaintext || id_key):
the official client rejects them ("detected chunk with wrong digest"),
and the bare digest gives the server a fingerprint of the plaintext.
Chunks now go through client.ChunkDigest, like the CLI and the machine
backup already did. Covered by TestChunkStateEncryptedDigests.

Snapshots already written that way (0.4.1, 0.4.2) stay restorable: on an
encrypted snapshot the DIDX reader also accepts the bare sha256 of the
decrypted chunk (still bound to the index; encrypted chunks have also
passed AES-GCM). proxmox-backup-client cannot read them: a new full
backup is needed for that. Covered by TestDIDXReaderAtLegacyEncrypted*.

No key in Service Mode: catalog, search, browse and restore run in the
GUI process with a ticket minted by the service, and that Config carried
no key file, so every read failed with "is encrypted but no encryption
key was provided". The ticket now carries the server's key file path
(not the key; the sanitized config already exposes it), with the
hydrated config as fallback for an older service, and the GUI unlocks it
like standalone mode does.

Token-only servers: minting the ticket needs the PBS user/password
stored next to the token (PBS issues no ticket for an API token); the
error now says so instead of "username and password are required to
obtain a ticket", and the misleading doc comment is fixed.
